                    "message": "Baseboard. Sorry, i just copy-pasted those diagrams from Olek's patch.\n\nI will adjust the wording to be more in entity-manager notation and not in terms of Redfish \ud83d\ude0a"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 86,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Oliver Brewka",
                        "email": "oliver.brewka@9elements.com",
                        "username": "mox669"
                    },
                    "message": "In general I am in favor of this design. It is very flexible, and - speaking for multi-host - covers all usecases. It gives room for extending the schema easily with further associations, i.e. 'cooling' / 'cooled_by'.\n \nHaving only a single 'Port' definition feels more intuitive too. The relationship between two items is well expressed with the PortType property on every Port record."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 86,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "I agree, it is a good enhancement."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 86,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks you for reviewing."
